---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import VentureDemo from '../components/VentureDemo.astro';
import {getArticles} from '../data/content';
const articles = (await getArticles()).filter(article => article.category === 'Research');
---
<Layout title='Research & experiments' description='Explore NRTH Labs experiments, manipulate our continuous form study, and read the questions behind NRTH research.'>
  <section class='page-intro'><span class='eyebrow'>NRTH Labs / Research journal</span><h1>A question is<br />a place to begin.</h1><p>Small experiments make an idea tangible. Explore the question, the method, and the limits of what a study can tell us.</p></section>
  <section class='section research-study' id='form-study'><div class='proof-intro' data-reveal><div><span class='eyebrow'>Design experiment / 001</span><h2>Continuity<br />in four strands.</h2></div><div><p>Can four independent contours keep a shared identity while their relationships change?</p><span class='eyebrow'>Published October 8, 2026 / Website design study</span></div></div><VentureDemo slug='nrth-labs' /><div class='study-notes' data-reveal><article><span class='eyebrow'>Method</span><h3>Keep the parts.</h3><p>Four equally sampled contours interpolate between rings and infinity. The sliders change their relationship and the viewing perspective without replacing the strands.</p></article><article><span class='eyebrow'>Observation</span><h3>The relationship matters.</h3><p>The endpoints remain identifiable, while intermediate poses introduce different crossings and silhouettes. Perspective reveals connections hidden in a flat view.</p></article><article><span class='eyebrow'>Limit</span><h3>A visual exploration.</h3><p>This is a website identity study, not a tested product capability or scientific result. It demonstrates continuous geometry; it does not establish a broader operational outcome.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class='section research-reading'><div><span class='eyebrow'>Research perspectives</span><h2>Record what<br />the question reveals.</h2><label class='research-search'><span class='sr-only'>Search research perspectives</span><input type='search' placeholder='Search perspectives' data-research-search /></label></div><div data-research-list>{articles.map(article => <a class='research-entry' href={'/insights/' + article.slug} data-research-entry data-search-text={(article.title + ' ' + article.description).toLowerCase()}><span class='eyebrow'>{article.category}</span><h3>{article.title}</h3><p>{article.description}</p><Icon /></a>)}<p data-research-empty hidden>No matching perspectives. Try another search.</p></div></section>
  <section class='section contact-section'><span class='eyebrow'>NRTH Labs</span><a class='contact-heading' href='/contact?project=nrth-labs'>Have a question<br />worth testing? <Icon name='upRight' /></a></section>
</Layout>
<script>document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-research-search]')?.addEventListener('input', event => {const query = (event.target as HTMLInputElement).value.trim().toLowerCase(); let count = 0; document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-research-entry]').forEach(entry => {entry.hidden = !entry.dataset.searchText?.includes(query); if (!entry.hidden) count++;}); document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-research-empty]')!.hidden = count > 0;});</script>
